<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie03f8137e494117b7a238e3af72527e0a46369e1" commit="2b1e4b3412af6e582dd4044f4fcb359335716eae" commit_message="g: add a function to report current board ID mismatch status  Until the Board ID check is moved to RO, it is possible to start an RW with a mismatching Board ID.  Let's add a function to check for mismatch and report the status.  Also eliminating the unnecessary check for empty header Board ID field - it is going to match any board ID anyways and fixing a CPRINTF statement in read_board_id().  BRANCH=cr50 BUG=b:35586335 TEST=verified that empty board ID header does not trigger a mismatch      on a board with a non-empty INFO1. With the rest of the patches      applied verified that board ID mismatch is reported properly.  Change-Id: Ie03f8137e494117b7a238e3af72527e0a46369e1 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/535975 Reviewed-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="535975" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/75/535975/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I161f39354e5523121e26e8ad84a791a8b06e5123" commit="4e06d839b21729a97d650fa7fe7494709d708834" commit_message="g: provide an API to set rollback counter to ensure rollback  with the board ID match happening in the RW we need to be able to set the rollback counter to a value which would guarantee a fallback during the next boot.  BRANCH=cr50 BUG=b:35586335 TEST=with the rest of the patches verified the ability to set the      counter to trigger a fallback on the next reboot.  Change-Id: I161f39354e5523121e26e8ad84a791a8b06e5123 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/535976 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="535976" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/76/535976/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I58d97de61dc446aaf1dd06b6e2b6bb426c14a172" commit="6e7f53d36f4b74748b850fd0f34476265349bf0c" commit_message="cr50: check for board ID match at startup  When starting up the Cr50 should check if this image is supposed to run on a chip with the board ID value read from INFO1.  If it is not supposed to run on this chip, and there is no rollback counter overflow, set the rollback counter to a value which will trigger a rollback and reboot.  If rollback counter has already exceeded the threshold - set a flag indicating that the image is running in the &quot;mismatch&quot; mode and continue.  BRANCH=cr50 BUG=b:35586335 TEST=with the rest of the patches applied verified both falling back       to an older image and continuing running with the flag set if       rollback is not possible.  Change-Id: I58d97de61dc446aaf1dd06b6e2b6bb426c14a172 Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/535977 Reviewed-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="535977" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/77/535977/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I063b8384b8a2923cfb547cead9fe1716b6f98b2e" commit="8d0f2d48eb6f7a977edafb580ec01165171e76b9" commit_message="cbuildbot: lakitu-st: add cbuildbot configuration for lakitu-st  CQ-DEPEND=CL:526314 BUG=b:62272706  TEST=The following two commands succeeded.      $ cbuildbot --local -p 'chromiumos/chromite' lakitu-st-release      $ sudo apt-get install python-mox &amp;&amp; cd chromite &amp;&amp; ./cbuildbot/chromeos_config_unittest  Change-Id: I063b8384b8a2923cfb547cead9fe1716b6f98b2e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/526313 Commit-Ready: Edward Jee &lt;edjee@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Edward Jee &lt;edjee@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="526313" owner_email="edjee@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/13/526313/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="7"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I041bc2c520995bbde6076dbeabdf9898dbc4f6b7" commit="0908c05bd7a4f0a3282f5cc5e68d29800cdfcd4d" commit_message="Resolve incompatibility with Zero-Touch Devices  Devices which use Zero-Touch Enrollment in Hands-Off mode automatically proceed through OOBE without waiting for user input. Because of this, the DUT checks for updates as part of OOBE, independent from the update checks triggered by the test. In the autoupdate_EndToEndTest, this causes the chain of events observed by the test to differ from what was expected. This CL introduces an alternative method of update verification in autoupdate_EndToEndTest to be applied to DUTs using Hands-Off Zero-Touch Enrollment, thereby making the test compatible with such DUTs.  BUG=chromium:710716 BUG=chromium:704104 BUG=b:62219369 TEST=Ran autoupdate_EndToEndTest.py and verified that it works. Ran in all 4 possible secenarios: Non-zero-touch image -&gt; zero-touch image non-zt img -&gt; zt img non-zt img -&gt; non-zt img zt img -&gt; zt img Also ran each case multiple times to check for nondeterminism or flakiness. It passed every time.  Change-Id: I041bc2c520995bbde6076dbeabdf9898dbc4f6b7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googleso